Welcome and Portfolio Overview Today I will walk through the Action Registry from a leadership view down to the day-to-day work and administration. The purpose is to give us a shared place to describe an action, identify its owner and intended outcome, review the proposal, track execution, and assess what happened. Every figure discussed today belongs to the visible scope and selected filters, not automatically to the entire company. The Executive Dashboard helps leadership prioritize the portfolio by showing Active Actions, On Track, At Risk, Overdue, and Goal Met[cite: 1, 2]. We also have the Current Review-Week Snapshot, which reflects the latest recorded states and dates, rather than an automatic historical comparison[cite: 1, 2].
Workspace Navigation and My Work The left navigation organizes the work by purpose[cite: 1, 2]. Submission & Updates is used to register and maintain actions, Approvals & Feedback brings together review decisions and comments, and Effectiveness & Decisions is where assessments and follow-ups are managed[cite: 1, 2]. We also have the Gantt view, which translates recorded start and target end dates into a timeline, and My Work, which helps users find relevant assigned work[cite: 1, 2]. My Work also contains explicit saved historical snapshots for comparable historical reviews[cite: 1, 2].
